1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,149
CareBuddy is our submission for the Tencent Cloud Healthcare Track,
case study two: AI Healthier Every Day.

2
00:00:07,149 --> 00:00:12,627
It is a mobile companion for everyday self-care and family care
between healthcare visits.

3
00:00:12,627 --> 00:00:17,628
Imagine a busy adult trying to remember their own routines while
helping Mom and Dad.

4
00:00:17,628 --> 00:00:23,976
CareBuddy brings the next task, useful care records, and an AI
assistant into one place.

5
00:00:23,976 --> 00:00:28,537
This walkthrough uses the live mobile website with fictional care
records.

6
00:00:28,537 --> 00:00:33,239
We will show an actual AI reminder change and its saved result.

7
00:00:33,239 --> 00:00:35,465
Explore the demo opens Today.

8
00:00:35,465 --> 00:00:43,246
Weather stays at the top, with Singapore temperature, humidity, and
PSI from public NEA and MSS feeds.

9
00:00:43,246 --> 00:00:46,923
Unhealthy PSI appears in red with a mask-up prompt.

10
00:00:46,923 --> 00:00:48,915
Rain adds an umbrella reminder.

11
00:00:48,915 --> 00:00:53,691
Below that, the next care task and daily progress make it easier to
act.

12
00:00:53,691 --> 00:01:00,092
Medication reminders, water, movement, and an evening wind-down stay
visible in the timeline.

13
00:01:00,092 --> 00:01:03,259
A recorded completion tells us what the user logged.

14
00:01:03,259 --> 00:01:08,221
An unfinished item does not prove that somebody missed a medication
dose.

15
00:01:08,221 --> 00:01:12,178
Review Sleep opens last night's duration and stage breakdown.

16
00:01:12,178 --> 00:01:16,825
Light, deep, and REM sleep each have a percentage and an explanation.

17
00:01:16,825 --> 00:01:21,199
A simple evening recommendation gives the user a practical next step.

18
00:01:21,199 --> 00:01:24,069
Sleep is currently fixed frontend content.

19
00:01:24,069 --> 00:01:31,376
Your Live Health shows blood pressure, pulse, temperature, and oxygen,
with breathing rate on the review page.

20
00:01:31,376 --> 00:01:36,900
Those readings come from the database through a backend API, but the
values are illustrative.

21
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,614
No wearable is connected.

22
00:01:38,614 --> 00:01:47,097
The distinction matters: an API refresh is a working feature, while a
connected measurement stream is a future integration.

23
00:01:47,097 --> 00:01:51,069
Family gives Me, Mom, and Dad separate care views.

24
00:01:51,069 --> 00:01:54,938
Selecting Mom changes the routines and appointments we work with.

25
00:01:54,938 --> 00:01:59,728
Her appointment has a preparation checklist and a clear confirmation
status.

26
00:01:59,728 --> 00:02:02,790
A saved appointment record is not a clinic booking.

27
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:09,040
Benefits shows recorded allowances and balances, with conditions and
provenance available for review.

28
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:14,657
These benefit records are also fictional, so the insurer must confirm
real coverage.

29
00:02:14,657 --> 00:02:22,675
The aim is to help a caregiver keep relevant information together and
prepare useful questions before a healthcare visit.

30
00:02:22,675 --> 00:02:24,772
Here is the core agent workflow.

31
00:02:24,772 --> 00:02:29,658
In Buddy, we asked: Change my wind-down reminder to nine p.m. daily.

32
00:02:29,658 --> 00:02:32,605
This was a real request to Tencent TokenHub.

33
00:02:32,605 --> 00:02:35,379
The model selected a supported reminder tool.

34
00:02:35,379 --> 00:02:41,636
The backend checked the selected person, permissions, schedule, and
current record before saving.

35
00:02:41,636 --> 00:02:44,972
Buddy now shows the new daily time and a Saved receipt.

36
00:02:44,972 --> 00:02:48,348
Returning to Today shows the same nine p.m. reminder.

37
00:02:48,348 --> 00:02:53,478
The application reports a successful change only after database
persistence.

38
00:02:53,478 --> 00:02:57,365
Request IDs prevent a retry from creating a second write.

39
00:02:57,365 --> 00:03:03,686
A missing field or an invalid action stops the save and asks the user
for the information needed.

40
00:03:03,686 --> 00:03:09,296
When the user asks for a routine GP consultation, Buddy offers the
WhiteCoat button.

41
00:03:09,296 --> 00:03:11,525
The user chooses whether to continue.

42
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:13,938
This opens an external care service.

43
00:03:13,938 --> 00:03:20,473
It does not claim a booking, verify insurance, or send the
conversation and readings to WhiteCoat.

44
00:03:20,473 --> 00:03:24,800
Clinical and medication concerns stay with qualified professionals.

45
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:28,257
Apparent emergencies follow a separate urgent-care route.

46
00:03:28,257 --> 00:03:34,311
Our focus is everyday care support, with clear limits on what this
companion can do.

47
00:03:34,311 --> 00:03:39,097
Settings also lets a user export a personal plugin for Codex or
Claude.

48
00:03:39,097 --> 00:03:43,228
They choose the people to include and whether to include health-
reading alerts.

49
00:03:43,228 --> 00:03:46,954
The exported skill connects to a scoped MCP endpoint.

50
00:03:46,954 --> 00:03:53,465
It can read new care notifications and acknowledge delivered alert
IDs, but cannot edit care records.

51
00:03:53,465 --> 00:03:55,936
Connections expire and can be revoked.

52
00:03:55,936 --> 00:04:00,154
Background checks begin only after installation and host scheduling.

53
00:04:00,154 --> 00:04:04,110
They read the latest stored data, including labelled demo readings.

54
00:04:04,110 --> 00:04:09,746
Delivery tracking suppresses unchanged repeat alerts, and quiet checks
stay quiet.

55
00:04:09,746 --> 00:04:14,767
This is scheduled support, not continuous emergency monitoring.

56
00:04:14,767 --> 00:04:17,948
The mobile interface uses React and TypeScript.

57
00:04:17,948 --> 00:04:23,564
Express and SQLite run behind HTTPS on a Tencent Cloud Ubuntu server.

58
00:04:23,564 --> 00:04:31,433
A private MCP connection assembles the selected person's reminder,
appointment, and benefit context for TokenHub.

59
00:04:31,433 --> 00:04:38,919
Prompts require grounded answers, preserve medication instructions,
and define allowed tools and care navigation.

60
00:04:38,919 --> 00:04:42,527
Code validates the model's proposed command independently.

61
00:04:42,527 --> 00:04:44,975
There is no arbitrary SQL tool.

62
00:04:44,975 --> 00:04:48,943
Our architecture deck shows these trust boundaries and trade-offs.

63
00:04:48,943 --> 00:04:52,638
Browser identity is a no-login prototype namespace.

64
00:04:52,638 --> 00:05:01,033
Verified accounts, real device feeds, and clinical evaluation remain
necessary before a patient deployment.

65
00:05:01,033 --> 00:05:05,784
We used CodeBuddy to refine the interface and investigate backend
onboarding.

66
00:05:05,784 --> 00:05:13,585
These genuine development screenshots show the requirements, source
reading, task planning, and colour and font work.

67
00:05:13,585 --> 00:05:20,270
A useful tip is to give the coding agent concrete acceptance criteria
and small file-specific tasks.

68
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:25,062
Check the mobile screen, the server response, and the persisted
record.

69
00:05:25,062 --> 00:05:30,239
Test retries, permissions, and failure paths as well as the happy
path.

70
00:05:30,239 --> 00:05:35,161
The verified reference release passed two hundred and forty-two
automated tests.

71
00:05:35,161 --> 00:05:37,694
We have not measured patient outcomes.

72
00:05:37,694 --> 00:05:48,930
A proposed pilot would compare routine-change time against manual
forms, aim for eighty percent unaided completion of key tasks, and
measure unwanted repeat notifications.

73
00:05:48,930 --> 00:05:57,733
CareBuddy's demonstrated value is a clearer next step and less work
to organise everyday and family care.
